(Regression test: Delete the file... had two bugs:
1. uses_files was never set, so file.asm was never included and
   FILE_DELETE was an undefined NASM macro - the program failed to
   assemble entirely.
2. Even if it had assembled, _last_error was never set after the
   syscall, so 'On error' after Delete the file would silently never
   fire even on genuine errors like ENOENT.)

(Error path: file doesn't exist -> On error must fire)
Delete the file "/tmp/vox_test_file_delete_regression_xyz".
On error print "error caught".

(Success path: delete an actually-existing file)
open a file for writing called tmpf at "/tmp/vox_test_file_delete_regression".
Close tmpf.
Delete the file "/tmp/vox_test_file_delete_regression".
On error print "BUG: delete failed on existing file", exit 1.
Print "deleted ok".

(Double-delete must error, not silently succeed)
Delete the file "/tmp/vox_test_file_delete_regression".
On error print "second delete error caught".
